{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I've [G]lived by the [D]river all my [G]life.
[G]Don't know [D]nothin but toil and [G]strife.
[G]Can't go home [C]again.
[D]Can't go home [G]again.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Well east and west the [D]highway roll.
[D]Lord have mercy [C]on my poor soul.
[C]I miss my blue eyed [Em]baby oh,
[G]My pretty little [D]blue eyed [G]baby oh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Well that river's deep, and that river's wide.
The devil stands on every side.
Can't go home again.
Can't go home again.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
That pretty little girl I love so well.
She goes to heaven, Lord, I go to hell.
Can't go home again.
Can't go home again.
{end_of_chorus}
